    "title": "I-81 Northbound in Schuylkill County reopen after tractor-trailer crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julia Priest ,\n2 hours ago\nSCHUYLKILL COUNTY (WBRE/WYOU) — Authorities say Interstate 81 Northbound in Schuylkill County has reopened after it was closed following a single tractor-trailer crash.\nSchuylkill County officials confirmed with 28/22 News units were called at about 6:40 p.m. to Interstate 81 Northbound near mile marker 132 for a reported single tractor-trailer crash.\nThe Delano Fire Company handled the response to the incident, authorities add.\nResidents react after Stroudsburg mayor steps down It’s unknown if anyone was injured or the extent of said injuries in the incident.\nThe Pennsylvania Department of Transportation (PennDOT) said all lanes of Interstate 81 Northbound between Exit 131A to PA 54 East, Hometown, and Exit 138 to PA 309, McAdoo/Tamaqua were closed.\nThe highway has since reopened at about 10:30 p.m., according to PennDOT.\nYou can stay up to date on speed limit restrictions, road conditions, and closures on 511PA.com .\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to 28/22 News.\n1",
